# Paths under the project root that travel with deploys.
# Used by scripts/gce-push-config.sh to overwrite the corresponding files on
# the VM's persistent data disk. State files (sessions, state, repositories,
# trivia plugin, etc.) are NOT in this list and stay untouched on the VM.
#
# Copy this file to data/.deploy-include (gitignored) and edit it to match
# your instance:
#   cp data/.deploy-include.example data/.deploy-include
#
# Format: one path per line, relative to the repo root. Lines starting with
# `#` and blank lines are ignored.

# Universal project-class paths (every Clack instance should push these)
data/config.json
data/mcp.json
data/default_configuration

# Per-instance project paths — uncomment / add lines below as needed.
# Plugins that ship code (an index.js + assets, no persistent state) go here.
# Plugins that have local state on the VM (e.g. trivia's question/score JSON)
# must NOT be listed here, or you will clobber their state on every push.
#
# Examples:
# data/plugins/my-org-plugin
# data/plugins/another-code-only-plugin

# NOTE: worker guardrail hooks need no entries here — the standard deploy
# (scripts/gce-update-image.sh) pushes data/worker-settings.json automatically,
# and hook binaries are baked into the image via data/docker/Dockerfile.custom.
# Full guide: docs/worker-settings.md
